.TH VEZ 1 "2026" "vez" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vez \- Svara's overlay-aware package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vez
[options]
.I command
[arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vez
is Svara's package manager. It speaks plain yum/dnf repository metadata
and resolves and applies transactions itself, without depending on dnf or
libdnf. On a booted Svara system, package operations are layered on top
of the read-only base image instead of modifying it directly, and the
layer is rebuilt at every boot so an installed package survives a reboot.
.PP
Vez does
.B not
ship a
.B dnf
or
.B dnf5
shim, so a script that calls dnf by name still calls dnf. Use
.B vez
directly.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are accepted before or after the command name and apply to
most subcommands.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to vez's main config file (dnf.conf compatible [main] section).
Default: /etc/vez/vez.conf.
.TP
.B \-\-repo\-dir \fIPATH\fR
Directory of dnf/yum style .repo files. Default: /etc/yum.repos.d.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-dir \fIPATH\fR
Directory where downloaded .rpm files are cached before install. Default:
/var/cache/vez.
.TP
.B \-y\fR, \fB\-\-assumeyes\fR
Assume "yes" to any prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-assumeno\fR
Assume "no" to any prompt.
.TP
.B \-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non essential output.
.TP
.B \-x\fR, \fB\-\-exclude \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude a package (by name, glob capable) from consideration. Repeatable,
comma separated.
.TP
.B \-C\fR, \fB\-\-cacheonly\fR
Run entirely from cached repo metadata; error instead of touching the
network.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\fR
Force a repo metadata refresh, ignoring metadata_expire.
.TP
.B \-\-repo\fR, \fB\-\-repoid \fIID\fR
Restrict operations to only these repo ids (glob capable, repeatable,
comma separated).
.TP
.B \-\-enablerepo\fR, \fB\-\-enable\-repo \fIID\fR
Enable a repo for this run only, even if disabled (glob capable,
repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-disablerepo\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-repo \fIID\fR
Disable a repo for this run only, even if enabled (glob capable,
repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gpgchecks\fR, \fB\-\-nogpgcheck\fR
Skip GPG signature verification entirely for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-setopt \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
dnf style config override, repeatable. vez only acts on
tsflags=noscripts (skip rpm scriptlets); other keys are accepted and
ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-allowerasing\fR
Allow removing conflicting or obsoleted packages to complete a
transaction, instead of refusing.
.TP
.B \-\-best\fR
Require the newest available version to resolve cleanly, rather than
silently falling back to an older one.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-unavailable\fR
Drop package names that don't match anything in the enabled repos
instead of failing the whole transaction. Only affects install.
.TP
.B \-\-repofrompath \fINAME,BASEURL\fR
Add an ad hoc repo from a name,baseurl pair, for this run only.
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-autoremove\fR, \fB\-\-noautoremove\fR
Don't remove now unneeded dependency only packages after a remove.
.TP
.B \-\-installroot \fIPATH\fR
Operate against an alternate root instead of the real /, same as
dnf/rpm's own \-\-installroot.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recommends\fR
Don't pull in weak dependencies (Recommends) for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-broken\fR
If the full requested install set can't be resolved together, drop
whichever names are responsible and proceed with the rest.
.TP
.B \-\-multilib\-all\fR
Install every distinct architecture build of a matched package side by
side, instead of just one.
.TP
.B \-\-forcearch \fIARCH\fR
Resolve and download for a different architecture than the host's.
.TP
.B \-\-from\-repo \fIID\fR
Restrict candidate resolution to packages from a specific repo id (glob
capable, repeatable). Unlike \-\-repo, every enabled repo's metadata is
still loaded for dependency checks.
.TP
.B \-\-from\-vendor \fIVENDOR\fR
Restrict candidate resolution to packages whose Vendor tag matches (glob
capable, repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-downloadonly\fR
Resolve and download the transaction, but don't apply it. Applies to
install, upgrade, downgrade, reinstall, distro\-sync, autoremove and
swap.
.TP
.B \-\-destdir \fIPATH\fR
With \-\-downloadonly, where to write the downloaded .rpms. Defaults to
\-\-cache\-dir.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-downgrade\fR
Allow resolving to an older version than what's currently installed.
This is the default; the flag exists for parity and explicitness.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-allow\-downgrade\fR
Forbid the resolver from downgrading anything to satisfy this request.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Resolve and install one or more packages. Aliases: in, pour. Accepts
comps style @group\-id and @^environment\-id names in addition to plain
package names.
.TP
.B remove\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Remove one or more packages. Aliases: rm, erase.
.TP
.B upgrade\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-advisory \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-security\fR] [\fB\-\-bugfix\fR] [\fB\-\-enhancement\fR] [\fB\-\-advisory\-severity \fILEVEL\fR]
Upgrade one or more installed packages to the newest available version.
Always overlay only: a base image package named explicitly is reported
instead of being layered into the overlay, since the base image is read
only. The one exception is \fBvez\fR itself, which is updated in place by
layering a copy into the overlay; the base image's copy is left untouched
underneath as the recovery. Aliases: up, update.
.TP
.B system\-upgrade\fR [\fIaction\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Mode aware system upgrade: dnf5's system\-upgrade on a plain host,
Svara's image update flow. On a plain host, a bare
invocation is an error; use one of the actions below to perform a major
release upgrade. On an overlay system, a bare invocation runs an
ordinary overlay package upgrade, then checks for and stages a new base
image.
.RS
.TP
.B download \fB\-\-releasever \fIVERSION\fR
Resolve and download the new release's packages without touching the
running system.
.TP
.B reboot
Stage the downloaded transaction and reboot into applying it.
.TP
.B clean
Discard a staged transaction.
.TP
.B log
Show the log of a past or current system upgrade run.
.TP
.B status
Show the status of a past or current system upgrade run.
.RE
.TP
.B reinstall\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Reinstall one or more installed packages at their exact current version.
Alias: rei.
.TP
.B downgrade\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Downgrade one or more installed packages to the newest available version
older than what's installed. Alias: dg.
.TP
.B distro\-sync\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Make installed packages exactly match the best available repo version,
upgrading or downgrading as needed. With no names given, every overlay
installed package is synced. Aliases: dsync, distrosync.
.TP
.B autoremove\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Remove overlay packages that were pulled in only as a dependency and are
no longer required by anything still installed.
.TP
.B swap \fIremove_spec\fR \fIinstall_spec\fR
Remove remove_spec and install install_spec as two back to back
transactions, approximating dnf's single transaction swap.
.TP
.B mark \fIaction\fR
Change a package's recorded install reason, controlling whether
autoremove may remove it later.
.TP
.B check\fR [\fB\-\-dependencies\fR] [\fB\-\-duplicates\fR] [\fB\-\-obsoleted\fR]
Check the installed package set for problems: unmet dependencies,
installed package conflicts, obsoleted packages, and duplicate name.arch
installs. With no flags, all checks run.
.TP
.B list\fR [\fIfilter\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-available\fR] [\fB\-\-extras\fR] [\fB\-\-obsoletes\fR] [\fB\-\-upgrades\fR] [\fB\-\-autoremove\fR] [\fB\-\-showduplicates\fR]
List installed packages, optionally filtered by a name substring. Lists
overlay installs by default; \-\-base lists the base image's package set
instead. Alias: ls.
.TP
.B search \fIquery\fR [\fB\-\-showrepo\fR]
Search enabled repos' package name and summary for a substring. Alias:
se.
.TP
.B provides \fIcapability\fR
Show what's installed or available that provides a capability (name,
versioned dependency, or file path). Alias: whatprovides.
.TP
.B check\-update\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
List installed packages that have a newer version available, without
downloading or installing anything. Alias: check\-upgrade.
.TP
.B repoquery\fR [\fIpattern\fR] [\fIoptions...\fR]
Query repo package metadata: name/glob matching, \-\-installed,
\-\-available, \-\-whatprovides, \-\-whatrequires, \-\-whatconflicts,
\-\-whatobsoletes, \-\-whatrecommends, \-\-whatenhances, \-\-whatsuggests,
\-\-whatsupplements, \-\-recursive, \-\-arch, \-\-duplicates, \-\-info,
\-\-queryformat/\-\-qf, \-\-requires, \-\-provides, \-\-conflicts, \-\-obsoletes,
\-\-recommends, \-\-enhances, \-\-suggests, \-\-supplements, \-\-srpm/\-\-source,
\-\-location, \-\-nvr, \-\-envra, \-\-extras, \-\-upgrades, \-\-querytags. Alias:
rq.
.TP
.B info \fIpackage\fR
Show detailed info (NEVRA, repo, summary) for a package name. Aliases:
if, more.
.TP
.B leaves
List overlay installed packages that nothing else installed depends on.
.TP
.B origin \fIpackage\fR
Show whether a package is installed, and if so from the base image or
the overlay.
.TP
.B paths
Print the overlay paths vez is using.
.TP
.B makecache
Unconditionally refresh cached repo metadata for every enabled repo.
Aliases: mc, makecache.
.TP
.B copr \fIaction\fR
Enable or disable a Copr repo.
.TP
.B clean\fR [\fIwhat\fR]
Clear cached data under \-\-cache\-dir. Default: all.
.TP
.B download\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-destdir \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-srpm\fR] [\fB\-\-releasever \fIVERSION\fR]
Resolve and download packages (and their dependencies) without
installing them.
.TP
.B debuginfo\-install\fR [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Install <name>\-debuginfo for one or more already named packages. Needs
the debuginfo packages to be present in a configured repo.
.TP
.B changelog\fR [\fIpackages...\fR]
Print the RPM changelog for one or more installed packages.
.TP
.B needs\-restarting
Scan running processes for ones using a shared library or binary that
was since deleted or replaced on disk, and report the affected PIDs.
.TP
.B repo \fIaction\fR
List or show details for configured repos.
.TP
.B history\fR [\fIaction\fR]
View recorded install and remove transactions. A bare invocation
defaults to list.
.TP
.B versionlock \fIaction\fR
Exclude packages from upgrade and distro\-sync candidate selection.
.TP
.B config\-manager\fR [\fB\-\-set\-enabled \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-set\-disabled \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-repo \fIID=BASEURL\fR] [\fIaction\fR]
Minimal .repo file editing: enable or disable existing repos, or add a
new one from a bare baseurl.
.TP
.B repoinfo \fIid\fR
Alias for "repo info".
.TP
.B repolist\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Alias for "repo list".
.TP
.B group \fIaction\fR
Comps group management: @id install syntax, group list, info, install
and remove.
.TP
.B environment \fIaction\fR
Comps environment management: @^id install syntax, environment list,
info, install and remove.
.TP
.B advisory \fIaction\fR
Security, bugfix and enhancement advisories (updateinfo). Not every
repo, especially third party ones, publishes this data. Alias:
updateinfo.
.TP
.B reposync\fR [\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-download\-path \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-newest\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-norepopath\fR]
Mirror a repo's packages to local disk. Respects the global \-\-repo
filter for which repo(s) to sync.
.TP
.B repomanage \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-keep \fIN\fR]
Prune old package versions from a local directory of .rpm files, grouped
by name and arch.
.TP
.B repoclosure\fR [\fB\-\-pkg \fIPATTERN\fR]
Report packages whose dependencies aren't satisfiable by anything in the
enabled repos.
.TP
.B builddep \fIspec\fR [\fB\-\-define \fINAME VALUE\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Install build dependencies from a .spec or .src.rpm file. Alias:
build\-dep.
.TP
.B automatic\fR [\fB\-\-timer\fR] [\fB\-\-downloadupdates\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-downloadupdates\fR] [\fB\-\-installupdates\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-installupdates\fR]
Non interactive upgrade suitable for a periodic timer or cron job,
driven by automatic.conf. Resolves an upgrade, optionally downloads it,
optionally applies it.
.TP
.B completions \fIshell\fR
Generate a shell completion script for vez.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vez/vez.conf
vez's main config file, dnf.conf compatible.
.TP
.I /etc/yum.repos.d/
Directory of .repo files.
.TP
.I /var/cache/vez
Downloaded package cache. Kept between runs so a replay can reinstall
without network access.
.TP
.I /var/lib/svara/vez/rpmdb
Vez's own rpm database, holding every package vez installed. Separate
from the base image's own database at
.IR /usr/share/rpm ,
which is read-only and belongs to the image. The two are unioned at query
time and never merged.
.TP
.I /var/lib/svara/vez/overlay/upper
The overlay upper directory. This is where an installed package's files
land, and because it is under
.I /var
they survive a reboot: the overlay itself is rebuilt from here on every
boot.
.TP
.I /var/lib/svara/vez/packages.list
The names vez installed, one per line. A replay reads this to restore the
layer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vez.conf (5),
.BR dnf.conf (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Svara project.
